 urday\, May 3rd and Sunday\, May 4th. Enjoy the spring weather with a leis
 urely stroll through the scenic trails at the EcoTarium or visit resident 
 species from otters to turtles to bald eagles. If you are feeling up for a
 n adventure\, hop on the open-air passenger train which offers a picturesq
 ue ride through the museum grounds. Additionally\, visit the Fitchburg Art
  Museum to view the special gallery\, Stephen DiRado\, Better Together: Fo
 ur Decades of Photographs\, which includes seventy-five black-and white ph
 otographs\, over 1\,000 projected color images\, and three videos about th
 e artist and his work process. WHEN: Saturday\, May 3rd and Sunday\, May 4
 th (+ the first full weekend of each month) WHERE: Learn something new thi
 s month with a visit to a participating cultural institution\, including: 
 EcoTarium\, 222 Harrington Way\, Worcester\, Mass. Fitchburg Art Museum\, 
 185 Elm Street\, Fitchburg\, Mass. WHY: Bank of America believes the arts 
 have a unique ability to connect people and communities and help local eco
 nomies thrive. Through Museums on Us\, Bank of America provides its cardho
 lders with free access during the first full weekend of every month to art
 istic and cultural experiences in Worcester County at celebrated instituti
 ons ranging from art\, children’s and history museums to aquariums\, bot
 anical gardens\, and science centers. This is one example of how the bank 
 strengthens the local communities it serves in\, creates greater cultural 
 understanding\, and expands accessibility to the arts. HOW: Use the bank
 ’s location finder tool to search for participating cultural attractions
 . Please check with our partners directly for current operating hours and 
 admission guidelines. Present your Bank of America\, Merrill or Bank of Am
 erica Private Bank credit or debit card along with a photo ID to gain free
  general admission to any participating institution during the first full 
 weekend (Saturday and Sunday) of each month. Cardholders only\; guests are
  not eligible for free admission. Program excludes fundraising events\, sp
 ecial exhibitions\, and ticketed shows. Not to be combined with other offe
 rs. Museum participation varies.\n\nSources: Discover Central Massachusett
 s\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/bank-of-america-mus
 eums-on-us%c2%ae-offers-free-admission-the-first-weekend-of-every-month/26
 157/
LOCATION:EcoTarium\, 222 Harrington Way\, Worcester\, MA\, 01604
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/bank-of-america-museums-on-us%
 c2%ae-offers-free-admission-the-first-weekend-of-every-month/26157/
