SUMMARY:Marble House Kid's Tour
DTSTART:20261013T000000
DTEND:20261013T020000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:ca6849e65d733cb5d269be45ea4657@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Our new audio Marble House Kids Tour\, designed for children u
 nder 13\, introduces kids to the great house from a unique and whimsical p
 erspective. A professional voice actor plays the role of Marble House – 
 Alva Vanderbilt’s “fourth child” – guiding guests from room to roo
 m\, telling stories in a friendly voice while meeting various characters a
 long the way\, like Apollo the Sun God\, who brags about his curly hair. H
 ear the Vanderbilt children laughing as they speak French during lunch in 
 the dining room. Enjoy the music of angels entertaining a collection of un
 likely neighbors\, including a lobster and a dragon. Listen to a news boy 
 excitedly yell “EXTRA\,” as he sells newspapers featuring a breaking s
 tory about Marble House during its construction. The Marble House Kids Tou
 r is available in English only.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https
 ://www.meetboston.com/event/marble-house-kids-tour/93741/
LOCATION:Newport Mansions\, 424 Bellevue Avenue\, Newport\, RI\, 02840
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/marble-house-kids-tour/93741/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nevermore: A Cask of Curious Things An Art Show by JMAC
DTSTART:20261014T000000
DTEND:20261101T000000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:c90791a0cd6a795cc1bdbd272e1050@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:From this JMAC presenter: From this JMAC presenter: ON DISPLAY
 : OCTOBER 14TH - NOVEMBER 1ST Inspired by the surrealist imagination of Ed
 gar Allan Poe\, Nevermore: A Cask of Curious Things invited artists to con
 tribute to an exhibition of strange treasures\, relics\, and collected won
 ders. Presented in collaboration with The Hanover Theatre Repertory's thea
 trical performances of monologues drawn from Poe’s writings\, this exhib
 ition explores the gothic allure of objects that carry stories: forgotten 
 trinkets\, fragments of memory\, peculiar keepsakes\, and artifacts that s
 eem to hum with mystery. Like the careful hoards made by ravens and other 
 corvids\, creatures known to gather curious and glittering things\, this e
 xhibition imagines a shadowed trove of collected relics\, each with its ow
 n quiet obsession. We sought artworks that evoke the feeling of opening a 
 hidden cask filled with enigmatic objects. Pieces may reflect themes of ob
 session\, memory\, loss\, devotion\, decay\, and the strange beauty of thi
 ngs kept and treasured. Artists are encouraged to interpret the gothic atm
 osphere of Poe’s world through objects that feel discovered\, collected
 \, or preserved.\n\nSources: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: h
 ttps://www.discovercentralma.org/event/nevermore%3a-a-cask-of-curious-thin
 gs-an-art-show-by-jmac/30982/
LOCATION:Jean McDonough Arts Center\, 20 Franklin St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 0
 1608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/nevermore%3a-a-cask-of-curious
 -things-an-art-show-by-jmac/30982/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Carved Images: Relief Printmaking
DTSTART:20261020T000000
DTEND:20261201T000000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:34628b748cc48f449127d00ec524b4@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Course Description: Relief is the oldest printmaking technique
  in the world\, with its origins dating back to at least 200 CE in China. 
 While materials and tools have evolved\, the general technique of carving 
 away negative space to create a raised image has remained the same. Studen
 ts will learn to work with basic techniques of making print blocks using v
 arious wood types and other types of substrates like linoleum. Once the ca
 rving or construction of the block is complete\, students will learn how t
 o effectively ink up and print their block on paper by hand printing and u
 sing an etching press. Students Should Bring: printmaking paper\, x-acto k
 nives\, gloves Dates: Weekly from October 20 - December 1 Meets: Tuesdays 
 from 6:00 PM to 9:00 PM\n\nSources: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent 
 page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/carved-images%3a-relief-prin
 tmaking/31042/
LOCATION:Worcester Center for Crafts\, 25 Sagamore Rd.\, Worcester\, MA\, 
 01605
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/carved-images%3a-relief-printm
 aking/31042/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Digital Photography 2
DTSTART:20261020T000000
DTEND:20261201T000000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:4b40d01034cf68e1fd800e11d6841b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Do you have some camera experience and are looking to grow as 
 a photographer? Look no further! Digital Photo 2 is for you! Take the next
  steps with your understanding of digital photography with "Digital Photog
 raphy II." In this course\, you will improve your use of manual settings w
 hile learning how to "see" when looking through the viewfinder of your cam
 era. Explore some of the many different types of photography such as portr
 ait\, landscape\, still life\, and abstraction\, as you become more confid
 ent with your choices of composition and visual content. You will improve 
 your digital workflow and learn basic photo editing skills using Adobe Pho
 toshop. Print-quality images will be created as students learn the basic s
 teps of preparing an image print. Students should be familiar with the bas
 ics of photography as well as the controls and functions of their digital 
 camera and will be assigned an iMac computer workstation accessible during
  class time. Perfect for those who have taken "Intro to Photography" or wa
 nt to improve their beginner skills in digital photography. It is requeste
 d all students provide a new\, unused memory card for their camera before 
 interfacing with computers in the lab. Materials fee will support ink and 
 paper for up to five test prints per/student Dates: Weekly from October 20
  - December 1 Meets: Tuesday from 6:30 PM - 9:30 PM\n\nSources: Discover C
 entral Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/
 introduction-to-digital-photography-2/31043/
LOCATION:Worcester Center for Crafts\, 25 Sagamore Rd.\, Worcester\, MA\, 
 01605
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/introduction-to-digital-photog
 raphy-2/31043/
END:VEVENT
