BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20261031T110000
DTEND:20261031T170000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:65e4079e81c88ba146e92e43ef76d0@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-10-31/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-10-31/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents: Members’ Fall Juried Show & Abstract A
 rtists of NE Exhibit
DTSTART:20261031T110000
DTEND:20261121T160000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:88e68e01499d90337396e2a0a53756@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:October 9\, 2026 FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE: Contact: Kelly Page\, 
 Gallery Manager kelly@newburyportart.org 65 Water St\, Newburyport MA 978-
 465-8769 Newburyport Art announces October Exhibitions October 10 – 31\,
  2026 Newburyport\, MA – Newburyport Art (NAA): announces the October ex
 hibitions at 65 Water\, including the Fall Juried Show\, the Abstract Arti
 sts Group of New England (AAGNE) Featured Interest Group Exhibition\, and 
 the Fall Gift Shop. There is a free opening reception and awards presentat
 ion on Saturday\, October 10 (4-6 PM)! The Fall Juried Show from October 1
 0th – 31st is an annual artist members’ exhibition that brings artists
  from around the region. Over 100 art pieces were selected from nearly 200
  entries and are on display on both floors of the gallery. Accepted media 
 include watercolor\, oils and acrylic\, gouache\, sculpture\, printmaking
 \, photography\, pastel\, mixed media and more. This year’s theme is ‘
 Making Moves\,’ which invites artists to explore the forces behind their
  creative practice. Juror Sarah LoVasco has a degree in Studio Art from th
 e University of Vermont and over twelve years’ experience in the retail 
 hardware business. Working with nationally renowned museums\, galleries\, 
 and corporate collections keeps Sarah up-to-date on industry best practice
 s and allows her a pipeline of resources for artwork and emerging artists.
  The NAA provides a gathering place for artists interested in meeting with
  other artists working in particular mediums\, by providing Featured Inter
 est Groups (FIGs). AAGNE (Abstract Artists of New England) was founded wit
 h a dual mission: to support\, encourage\, and promote abstract and non-tr
 aditional artists\; and to educate the public about their work. The artist
 s of AAGNE work in a variety of media\, approaches\, and styles. They are 
 brought together by a common interest: a fascination and passion for the a
 bstract elements in all art\, for Abstract art\, and art of abstraction. A
 lmost two dozen artists have their artwork shown in the first-floor Hills 
 gallery. Gallery Hours: Wednesday through Sunday from 11am-5pm. The galler
 y is handicap accessible. More information\, as well as an online gallery
 \, is available at newburyportart.org. Founded in 1948\, Newburyport Art i
 s dedicated to promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing a
 rt education and access to the visual arts for the entire community.\n\nSo
 urces: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/newbur
 yport-art-presents-members-fall-juried-show-abstract-artists-of-ne-exhibit
 /2026-10-31/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-members-fall-
 juried-show-abstract-artists-of-ne-exhibit/2026-10-31/
END:VEVENT
