BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Food Workshop: Celebrate the Cranberry
DTSTART:20261114T100000
DTEND:20261114T123000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:7345b7d369e7e4a435c914c77e50f7@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:With Thanksgiving on the horizon\, it’s time to celebrate th
 e cranberry. Hancock Shakers gathered cranberries in a bog near the North 
 Family and kept them for use all winter long. This year’s workshop will 
 focus on pear-cranberry jam and/ apple cranberry compote just in time for 
 you to plan your Thanksgiving menu. You’ll work in the Brick Dwelling Ki
 tchen. Suitable for ages 14 and up.\n\nSources: The Berkshires\nEvent page
 : https://berkshires.org/events-old/food-workshop-celebrate-the-cranberry/
LOCATION:Hancock Shaker Village\, 1843 West Housatonic Street\, Pittsfield
 \, MA\, 01201
URL:https://berkshires.org/events-old/food-workshop-celebrate-the-cranberr
 y/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20261114T110000
DTEND:20261114T170000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:724d0b32839c3d0025f908383c1118@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-11-14/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-11-14/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noguchi and Japanese American Internment During World War II
DTSTART:20261114T130000
DTEND:20261114T150000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:60dbef6247e8dfd14d6e78f1e94889@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join curator and scholar Christina Hiromi Hobbs for a talk exa
 mining Isamu Noguchi’s voluntary incarceration at the Poston War Relocat
 ion Center in Arizona during World War II. Hobbs will discuss Noguchi’s 
 complex motivations for entering the camp\, discuss its impact on his life
  and work and examine the historical context of art making during Japanese
  American incarceration. After the bombing of Pearl Harbor in 1941\, more 
 than 120\,000 people of Japanese ancestry were incarcerated in internment 
 camps created on U.S. soil. Many lived there for the duration of the war. 
 Read more about their stories — and why their experiences still matter t
 oday — from the Densho documentation project and Poston Preservation.\n
 \nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/no
 guchi-and-japanese-american-internment-during-world-war-ii/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/noguchi-and-japanese-american-internme
 nt-during-world-war-ii/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Remembrance Altars
DTSTART:20261114T103000
DTEND:20261114T120000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:e23bb213324bd972c333dfc5e1b059@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:From the ofrendas of Dia de los Muertos to butsudan in Japanes
 e Buddhist homes\, many different cultures create spaces for honoring ance
 stors. As the days grow shorter\, join us for a reflective art workshop th
 at reflects on those who came before us. Through simple mixed-media assemb
 lage\, participants will create a personal altar or remembrance piece that
  celebrates family\, chosen family\, mentors\, cultural heritage or loved 
 ones who have shaped their lives. No prior art experience is needed. All m
 aterials will be provided\, and participants are invited to bring copies o
 f photographs or small paper mementos they may wish to incorporate into th
 eir artwork. Studio Saturdays is a series of adult art making classes desi
 gned to inspire creativity and connection through multimedia arts explorat
 ion. Each class includes an arts activity that will inspire collaboration
 \, curiosity and creativity\, culminating in a completed individual artwor
 k and communal sharing.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://n
 orthofboston.org/event/remembrance-altars/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/remembrance-altars/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toy Story
DTSTART:20261114T110000
DTEND:20261114T140000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:ab1d30b73f2f6fc9a03a09dbc3340d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:When their owner is away\, Woody\, Buzz Lightyear\, and the re
 st of the toys come to life for an unforgettable adventure. As rivalry tur
 ns into friendship\, the two unlikely heroes must work together to find th
 eir way home. Pixar’s beloved original Toy Story is a timeless family cl
 assic filled with humor\, heart\, and imagination.\n\nSources: North of Bo
 ston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/toy-story/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/toy-story/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yin Yu Tang: A Chinese Home Tour
DTSTART:20261114T111500
DTEND:20261114T161500
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:ce2a4d6e105fdb1b2c8a44530b1590@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a 200-year-old Chinese home in Salem to experience
  Chinese art\, architecture and culture. For 200 years\, Yin Yu Tang stood
  in the rural village of Huang Cun in a mountainous region of southeastern
  China. Home to eight generations of the Huang family\, this house was dis
 mantled\, transported and re-erected at the Peabody Essex Museum in 2003 t
 hrough a partnership between PEM and the governmental authorities of Huizh
 ou\, in Anhui Province. Yin Yu Tang’s journey constitutes a landmark col
 laboration between Chinese and American architects\, artisans\, conservato
 rs\, engineers and museum experts. The home is presented as it was when th
 e family last lived there in 1982. Plan Your Visit Exercise care Please he
 lp us preserve the house for future generations by refraining from touchin
 g objects and the structure itself. Non-flash photography and videography 
 is permitted for personal use only. Tripods and selfie sticks are not allo
 wed. Please walk with care and watch out for uneven stonework and raised t
 hresholds. Store your belongings\, but keep your coat Yin Yu Tang is parti
 ally outdoors and may be cool in fall and winter. Strollers\, bags\, backp
 acks and umbrellas are not permitted in the house. Please leave them at th
 e coatroom or the cubbies by the Information desk. Our staff at the entran
 ce of the house can look after strollers. Pick up your audio guide in adva
 nce Please pick up your complimentary audio guide\, available in English a
 nd Mandarin\, at the Information desk 10 minutes before your visit. Please
  note: Plan to bring your own pair of headphones. Before your visit\, pres
 s #50 to listen to an introduction to the house. Once inside\, look for st
 one blocks with two-digit numbers. Press the number plus the play > button
  to hear the audio. Be prompt Please be at the doors to Yin Yu Tang five m
 inutes before your scheduled visit with your audio guide in hand. A staff 
 member will alert you shortly before the end of your time slot.\n\nSources
 : North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang
 -a-chinese-home-tour/2026-11-14/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang-a-chinese-home-tour/2026-1
 1-14/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Amesbury Open Studios
DTSTART:20261115T100000
DTEND:20261115T170000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:3b2efe85b493c1b05cbf3eb85d316e@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Come visit the historic town of Amesbury when over 100+ artist
 s open their studios and artwork for the public to enjoy\, buy and also cr
 eate! Here at 14 Cedar Street Studios\, we have over 20+ artists\, Kaha Co
 ffee\, Kitchen Local and all kinds of musical artists. Our studio will be 
 buzzing with action November 14th from 10-5pm and November 15th from 11-4p
 m. FREE trolley provided by the amazing Amesbury Cultural Council will bri
 ng you around town to all the stops.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent pa
 ge: https://northofboston.org/event/amesbury-open-studios/2026-11-15/
LOCATION:14 Cedar Street Studios\, 14 Cedar Streeet\, Amesbury\, MA\, 0191
 3
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/amesbury-open-studios/2026-11-15/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beauport Boutique’s Annual Sip & Shop
DTSTART:20261115T140000
DTEND:20261115T180000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:cf949a8b7cb930dfca5463732307d3@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Get a head start on your holiday shopping or find something sp
 ecial just for you at our annual Sip & Shop at the Beauport Boutique! Join
  us on Sunday\, November 15th from 2:00PM–6:00PM for a festive afternoon
  of shopping\, sipping\, and seasonal inspiration. Browse Beauport Boutiqu
 e favorites alongside special guest vendors while enjoying a glass of bubb
 ly and passed light bites. Whether you’re checking off your holiday list
  or treating yourself to something new\, spend the afternoon shopping by t
 he sea.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org
 /event/beauport-boutiques-annual-sip-shop/
LOCATION:Beauport Hotel Gloucester\, 55 Commercial Street\, Gloucester\, M
 A\, 01930
