BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haley Heynderickx
DTSTART:20261212T193000
DTEND:20261212T210000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:5afc479906210b270c81345f4f148b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Following the release of her acclaimed debut I Need to Start a
  Garden and its long-awaited follow-up Seed of a Seed\, Haley Heynderickx 
 recently released What of Our Nature\, a collaboration with Max García Co
 nover. After a year of touring with Max and working on new material\, she 
 now returns to the road for a rare run of solo performances. One of contem
 porary folk’s most quietly captivating voices\, Heynderickx writes with 
 warmth\, wit and self-reflection. Her songs find wonder in the everyday wh
 ile exploring questions of identity\, belonging and our relationship with 
 the natural world. Tender\, thoughtful and quietly spellbinding\, these sh
 ows are an invitation to step into the unknown with her and leave a little
  room for what may come next.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: htt
 ps://northofboston.org/event/haley-heynderickx/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/haley-heynderickx/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Holidays & Wintertide
DTSTART:20261212T200000
DTEND:20261212T220000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:c8dba8f4207f74a1b6afb9801bfd43@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:21+\, Positive I.D. Required Join Chris Langathianos\, Joe Wil
 kins\, Renee Dupuis\, Joe Cardoza\, & Dennis Monagle for a holiday season 
 tradition at The Cut on Saturday\, December 12th at 8pm. Enjoy the sounds 
 of the season\, the sounds of winter\, and other fun – and funny – sur
 prises in this annual holiday tradition. ABOUT CHRIS AND JOE Winners of th
 e 2020 New England Songwriting Competition for their song\, “Your Town (
 is Gonna Change)\,” Chris + Joe (Chris Langathianos and Joe Wilkins) are
  a Cape Ann-based duo with deep roots in the Greater Boston music scene\, 
 are known for their tight harmonies\, thoughtful songs\, and engaging bant
 er. Joe\, a multi-instrumentalist\, expert songwriter\, and producer\, tea
 med up with vocalist and live show producer\, Langathianos\, in 2013 and t
 hey have continued to capture audiences with their easy and melodic\, yet 
 diverse\, style\, witty banter and approachable sets. From easy melodic fo
 lk to contemporary pop and rock\, Chris + Joe bring a new twist to old fav
 orites\, mixed with deeply personal\, award-winning originals\, and a side
  of self-deprecating audience give-and-take. ABOUT RENEE & JOE Renee & Joe
  is a folk/rock duo whose music features both high energy vocal and instru
 mental arrangements as well as minimalist themes and gentle harmonies. The
 y’ve released three full length albums since 2014 and can be seen playin
 g around Cape Ann and greater New England as a duo and as a part of other 
 musical ensembles. Renee (piano/vocals) & Joe (bass/guitar/vocals) also pl
 ay in the neo-soul\, cabaret band What Time Is It Mr. Fox?. They live on C
 ape Ann with their two children.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: 
 https://northofboston.org/event/holidays-wintertide/
LOCATION:The Cut\, 177 Main Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/holidays-wintertide/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Middle Street Walking Tour
DTSTART:20261212T110000
DTEND:20261212T120000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:a5c4b99cf9c8c955cf89563e603eb0@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:A street with a remarkable history! Join a Cape Ann Museum doc
 ent for a fascinating stroll along historic Middle Street in downtown Glou
 cester. Discover the people\, places\, and events that shaped this iconic 
 neighborhood. Tours begin in the Cape Ann Museum lobby\, last approximatel
 y 45 minutes\, and are offered twice during the day at 11:00 a.m. and 1:00
  p.m. The Museum is free and open to the public all day\, making it the pe
 rfect destination for holiday fun. Create festive ornaments\, explore insp
 iring exhibitions\, tour historic Middle Street\, and celebrate the season
  with family and friends. Be sure to visit the Museum Store\, stocked with
  a distinctive selection of holiday gifts for everyone on your list. Cape 
 Ann Museum members receive 10% to 20% off purchases\, so it’s a great ti
 me to join or renew your membership. The Cape Ann Museum is proud to partn
 er with the Middle Street Walk\, inviting visitors to enjoy a full day of 
 festive activities\, history\, shopping\, and holiday cheer in the heart o
 f downtown Gloucester.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://no
 rthofboston.org/event/middle-street-walking-tour/2026-12-12/1/
LOCATION:Cape Ann Museum\, 27 Pleasant Street\, Gloucester\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/middle-street-walking-tour/2026-12-12/
 1/
END:VEVENT
