BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Albert Lee with Special Guests The Cryers
DTSTART:20270119T200000
DTEND:20270119T220000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:7cbfa4e191cf731251df61bf2f071b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Albert Lee “Lay It Down” tour is on its way. Albert is
  back out on the road in 2026 and 2027 performing tracks from his newest a
 lbum\, “Lay It Down” recorded at the legendary Konk Studios in London.
  Double Grammy winner with Earl Scruggs and Brad Paisley\, Albert Lee has 
 played with everyone from Jerry Lee Lewis to Eric Clapton\, to the Everly 
 Brothers to Emmylou Harris. He was a member of The Crickets in the post-Bu
 ddy Holly era\, and forged an impressive solo career along the way. From M
 ark Knopfler’s blistering Setting Me Up to Jimmy Webb’s soaring piano 
 ballad Too Young To Die\, to The Everly Brothers’ storming hit The Price
  Of Love\, Albert’s latest album sees his triumphant return to the studi
 o\, recording live\, as one of the greatest guitarists ever. Don’t miss 
 the man known as “Mr. Telecaster\,” one of the legendary guitarists of
  rock and roll\, rockabilly and country music. “The ultimate virtuoso. H
 is skill is extraordinary\, his ear is extraordinary and he’s gifted on 
 just about every level.” – Eric Clapton “When Saint Peter asks me to
  chronicle my time down here on earth\, I’ll be able to say – with pri
 de if that’s allowed – that for a while I played rhythm guitar in a ba
 nd with Albert Lee.” – Emmylou Harris “Albert is one of the most tal
 ented\, all-around musicians I’ve ever met- sings\, writes\, and he’s 
 also an accomplished keyboard player. Add humble\, self-effacing and good-
 natured\, and you have a great role model for the journeyman player. “
 – Dave Edmunds\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofb
 oston.org/event/albert-lee-with-special-guests-the-cryers/
LOCATION:The Cut\, 177 Main Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/albert-lee-with-special-guests-the-cry
 ers/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Homeschool Adventures: Session 1
DTSTART:20270119T130000
DTEND:20270119T160000
DTSTAMP:20261030T171909Z
UID:55f5427916813207762e3bbb226fa9@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Young explorers are invited to join us in September & October 
 for a 4-part homeschool series that will get them active & moving with nat
 ure adventures\, exercise\, and outdoor skill building. While exploring Ap
 pleton Farms & the Crane Estate\, participants complete active adventures 
 & design challenges that will exercise both their body & mind. Some potent
 ial activities include kayaking\, tide pooling\, wetland exploration\, ori
 enteering\, gardening\, obstacle course design\, and more! This is a drop-
 off program that is open to ages 5-11 and will include small group activit
 ies based on age and peer mentoring opportunities between age groups. The 
 class takes place rain or shine\, with as much time spent outdoors as poss
 ible. Students should arrive dressed for the weather and bring a lunch and
  water bottle. Homeschool Adventures: Session 1- This 4-class series progr
 am takes place on Tuesday afternoons from 1-4pm on September 15\, 22\, 29 
 & October 6. September 15: Tidepool & Shoreline Exploration at the Crane E
 state September 22: Kayaking Adventure at the Crane Estate September 29: P
 onding & Invasive Species Management at Appleton Farms October 6: Obstacle
  Course Design Challenge at Appleton Farms Tuition for the 4 classes is $2
 75 for Trustees Members and $325 for nonmembers. Registration covers all l
 isted session dates.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://nort
 hofboston.org/event/homeschool-adventures-session-1/2027-01-19/
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/homeschool-adventures-session-1/2027-0
 1-19/
END:VEVENT
